# Music -- what the player may NAME.
#
# READ-ONLY. A player does not write: no library database, no play counts, no
# transcoding. Declaring that makes it a property of the process rather than of
# today's code.
#
# Every prefix must be one the SESSION can already name, because the kernel
# resolves them in the PARENT's namespace at spawn -- a prefix the desktop does
# not hold is not a narrower grant, it is a spawn that fails with -2 before the
# program loads. The session holds ro /system, ro /data/apps, rw /home/<user>,
# rw /run. Photos learned this the hard way by asking for /data/pictures.

ro /system                  # its font and chrome resources
ro $HOME                    # the music, in $HOME/Music
